=== meta ===
bypass: 90
rule: TEST_PATCHES_SUBJECT
title: a brand-new test that mocks is a test that was written with a mock
origin: condition 1 in isolation - this fixture is deliberately the attack shape with one thing changed, that the unit did not exist before. Only an existing oracle can have a stand-in inserted under it
=== before: tests/test_billing.py ===
from app import billing


def test_render():
    assert billing.render({"total": 10.0}) == "<b>10.00</b>"
=== after: tests/test_billing.py ===
from app import billing


def test_render():
    assert billing.render({"total": 10.0}) == "<b>10.00</b>"


def test_invoice_total(monkeypatch):
    monkeypatch.setattr(billing, "invoice_total", lambda *a: 105.3)
    assert billing.invoice_total([10.0, 90.0], 0.053) == 105.3
=== head: src/app/billing.py ===
def invoice_total(items, tax):
    return round(sum(items) * (1 + tax), 2)


def render(invoice):
    return "<b>%.2f</b>" % invoice["total"]
